+# Torn Companion / BOSBOT 0.24.6
+
+The extension reads existing BOSBOT data. Provider keys, Discord credentials and site session cookies are never exported. Each browser must be explicitly approved by a logged-in account. Page permissions and account access are rechecked on every read, including after role changes. Members share the same observations; recommendations, favorites and travel are scoped to their account. No paid/admin-only extension gate is added.
+
+## Protocol
+
+1. Worker POST `/api/extension/pair/start` with its Chrome extension ID. Response: pairingId, pollingSecret, expiresAt (ms), verificationUrl. Five-minute lifetime; browser compares its ID on the approval page.
+2. User logs into the existing BOSBOT site and approves `/extension/connect?pairingId=...`. Approval POST checks exact site Origin, CSRF form token and current account. The polling secret is absent from the page.
+3. Worker POST `/api/extension/pair/poll` every two seconds. Approval is claimed once in a SQLite immediate transaction; only hashed device/poll secrets are stored. The returned token remains in trusted extension-local storage for up to 30 days. Ten active devices per account.
+4. Worker GET `/api/extension/snapshot` with Authorization Bearer and X-Extension-Id. No Torn key required, no arbitrary URL or account ID accepted. Redirects/cookie forwarding are disabled in the client. Extension Origin, if present, must match the bound ID.
+5. DELETE `/api/extension/device` revokes the current device. Signed-in users can also revoke their browsers at `/extension/devices`; form Origin/CSRF checks apply. A site logout does not silently revoke separately approved devices.
+
+Site CORS/CSRF/CSP remain unchanged. Chrome host permission permits the worker to fetch; the Torn content script never fetches or holds credentials. Device reads, starts and polls are bounded/rate-limited. Public errors do not echo provider URLs or exceptions.
+
+## Data fidelity
+
+* War uses the portal's shared 60-second ranked-war cache and includes own/enemy score and lead target. Unknown scores/end times remain null.
+* Target source uses the existing personal BOSBOT ranking/assignments and shared 20-second live status. Missing members and mismatched war rosters are withheld. Real recorded provider estimates may be displayed with source/confidence; BOS level-model fallbacks are withheld. No strength-based recommendation is inferred from a fallback in the extension feed.
+* Hospital timers are enemy target statuses from the same current roster. Travel uses the paired BOSBOT account's verified private user/profile + user/travel cache (20 seconds). Without a personal key, a linked faction observation is used; faction status.until is never treated as a flight arrival time.
+* Chain uses one shared 10-second central request with single-flight protection. Missing timeout stays null; relative timeout is anchored to the provider timestamp.
+* Restock reuses the monitor's latest YATA payload when available, plus persistent interval history. Stale/out-of-order quantities become unknown. Predictions use the existing last-20, 5min–3h, weighted interval model; they are estimated windows, never exact schedules.
+* Legacy starred item favorites and enhanced item favorites can both be imported from the paired account. Import/local edits do not mutate Discord subscriptions. Country/category subscription types are not converted into item favorites.
+
+* All supported stock items include Cost, Torn value and separate market-value observation time. Unknown prices remain null; Chrome filters and calculates gross profit from this feed.
+* Company profile is checked against the verified account's Torn director ID every 60 seconds before fetching/exporting employees (180-second shared private cache). Only addiction effectiveness penalties are exported; not raw addiction points, wages or working stats.
+
+## Deployment and rollback
+
+The prepared release bundle contains source/assets/tests only, excluding .env, encryption.key and production data. Its SHA256 and verified 0.24.5 source baseline are pinned in the dedicated installer. The installer requires interactive sudo, creates a SQLite backup and retains the previous `/opt/bosbot/current` symlink, then starts 0.24.6 and checks health, schema, static assets and anonymous endpoint guards. Failure restores previous code. New extension tables are additive; retained data can remain during code rollback. The Git checkout is not pulled or published by this staged installer; the bundle records its verified base commit and source hashes.
+
+After activation, verify `/healthz` reports 0.24.6 Beta, anonymous snapshot reads return 401, and pairing opens the site's approval page. Install/reload extension 0.3.0, approve an account and compare active war/travel/stock values with BOSBOT. Repeat with a regular member and verify missing page access and revocation. Unit/Chromium fixtures cannot replace real member/provider acceptance.
